[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/698","id":4469437954,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWoOrs8AAAABCmY2Ag","html_url":"https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv/pull/698","diff_url":"https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv/pull/698.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv/pull/698.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/issues/698","number":698,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix variable expansion in dotenv run --no-override","user":{"login":"ROTl24","id":119035617,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxhW4Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119035617?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24","html_url":"https://github.com/ROTl24","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #697.\r\n\r\nWith `dotenv run --no-override`, a variable keeps its existing environment value, but references to it still expand using the value in `.env`. For example, the child process can receive `BASE=environment` alongside `DERIVED=file/suffix`.\r\n\r\nThis change passes the CLI's `override` option to `DotEnv`, which already handles both expansion orders. References now use the same precedence as the variables passed to the child process.\r\n\r\nThe regression test launches a real child process and checks both values. It covers the default mode, `--override`, and `--no-override`, with the existing variable absent, nonempty, or empty. The two conflicting `--no-override` cases fail without the fix.\r\n\r\nValidation: 214 tests passed and 50 were skipped on Windows with Python 3.13.15. The existing tests need `printenv`, so Git for Windows' `usr/bin` was included in the test process PATH. All nine upstream CI jobs also passed on Linux and Windows.\r\n\r\n\r\n","created_at":"2026-09-08T02:15:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T03:05:57Z","closed_at":"2026-09-30T03:05:57Z","merged_at":"2026-09-30T03:05:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"e0310e5bb3f2b701b11bbc007ca0c82c1bd56f38","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/698/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/698/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/issues/698/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theskumar/python-dotenv/statuses/524f1455c2925c650607968fa3dab649b6a7a9e1","head":{"label":"ROTl24:fix/cli-no-override-interpolation","ref":"fix/cli-no-override-interpolation","sha":"524f1455c2925c650607968fa3dab649b6a7a9e1","user":{"login":"ROTl24","id":119035617,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxhW4Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119035617?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24","html_url":"https://github.com/ROTl24","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ROTl24/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.c